{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer","id":1499047,"title":"Embracing a sorcerer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-07T03:12:14-08:00","id":1499047,"title":"Embracing a sorcerer","content":"I'm not sure how to do this but now I've got a game coming up where it's an issue, so I'm going to need a rule on it. Do they keep their paths as a separate ability paid for with out of clan costs? Do I translate it to equivalent thaumaturgical paths? Do they just lose sorcery altogether? I think they just loose it, as Sorcerers and Mages who became clans generally used their knowledge to build new blood sorcery disciplines, like Thaumaturgy and Necromancy, so should that translate to not having your mortal sorcery but gaining an affinity for an equivalent vampiric sorcery/path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T03:37:21-08:00","id":1499048,"title":"","content":"There's never been an official answer on how exactly to handle this.<br /> <br /> Technically, if you Embrace a sorcerer, they lose their Paths and sucks to be them. However, in the past the books have recognized that this is not fun for most games where the sorcerer is either a PC or a central NPC. The usual solution is to convert the sorcerer's Paths into XP (or freebies) they can then use on Disciplines and supernatural Merits that help replicate some of their previous mystic skills and affinities. <br /> <br /> From a dramatic/narrative standpoint, it usually a good idea to avoid blood sorcery and necromancy during this conversion to help keep to the idea that the Embrace is a massive shock to the system and the now fledgling is going to have to relearn their former skills over time via training in blood magic. Focusing on common Disciplines and Merits is better for the idea that the Embrace shaped some of that magical affinity into a vampiric form. A sorcerer skilled in scrying having Auspex, or mental magic gaining dots in Dominate and Presence for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T04:36:32-08:00","id":1499052,"title":"","content":"It depends on the ST. Revised Sorcerer basically pointed out that if ST is OK with it there is no reason not to have them keep Sorcerer Paths. But if they aren't, I suggest just converting their Paths to XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T04:44:36-08:00","id":1499054,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26836_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26836\" data-vbnamecard=\"26836\">Rhywbeth</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T06:06:24-08:00","id":1499058,"title":"","content":"I play it similar to Technoma's option. That's because I treat some sorcery paths as being learnable (or duplicatable) by vampires and vice versa.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T07:24:53-08:00","id":1499060,"title":"","content":"My standpoint is that most mortal sorcery paths are <i>fine</i> as blood magic paths and basically should be left alone. Other are more complicated and need to be addressed on an case by case biases. For example the classic &quot;hellfire&quot; path has several different ways it can do damage. If a sorcerer has multiple of these then convert it over to lure of flames, path of levinbolt etc, as needed. <br /> <br /> Likewise I don't think that vampires should be able to heal, (the exception are the Salubri but that is their deal.) So the 'Path of Healing' just shouldn't be available to the Blood Sorcerer in question even if they had it in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T09:19:43-08:00","id":1499069,"title":"","content":"My take is that if vampires can perform normal sorcery then it invalidates the idea of Blood Magic because it is a needless duplicate. Why invent it at all if Tremere (or any other mortal magician) could keep using their old Sorcery Paths anyway?<br /> <br /> Originally the entire idea behind the Tremere was that they knew magic was going to die, and wanted to preserve their powers in a more hostile environment to magic. That was kind of achieved when Mage established the idea of Paradox. But the proliferation of Sorcery Paths (especially Paths that have effects that would clearly be impacted by Paradox if it was Sphere magic) really invalidated that. Now saying that Sorcery Paths can just be used by vampires really make the entire Tremere backstory incredibly stupid - not just that they became vampires to preserve their magical abilities, but also the idea that they had to relearn everything and recreate new ways to perform those tasks.<br /> <br /> Having said that, most Blood Sorcery Paths and Sorcery Paths are either the same mechanically or practically the same. It should not be that hard for the new vampire to &quot;relearn&quot; how to do the same magic, but now using vitae as its source of magical power. It will just take a certain amount of study and effort, and if you have access to an existing body of knowledge (like the Tremere do), that learning curve will not be long.<br /> <br /> For NPCs, I'd strip them of their Sorcery Paths and force them to relearn what they want to do as Thaumaturgy. If they are among the Tremere or some other organization that can assist with that, they should be able to adapt very quickly. If they are on their own, it may take them years, decades, or longer to relearn everything. That is mainly just flavor and setting detail.<br /> <br /> But what about for PCs? PCs don't want to lose the XP they invested, start from scratch, and so on. It won't seem fair to them. In their case, I'd translate any Sorcery Path they knew to their Blood Magic equivalent. If there is not an equivalent, then they lose that Path, but I'd refund them the XP they lost by that. While I would want to provide an IC explanation for them &quot;relearning&quot; their Sorcery to Thaumaturgy, I would not want to waste time in the game to do so, and would want to keep them happy as a player. So I'd talk it over with the player to see what we could come up. Ideally there would be certain amount of time in terms of preludes before he starts playing the game, downtime activity, or perhaps a schedule where after so much time IC certain powers could come back online if the player is willing. But if the player does not want to roleplay that and simply have access to his powers immediately, I'd bite the bullet and make him happy.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, in my own chronicles I rule that Sorcery Paths whose effects would be something that would invalidated by Paradox if it was Sphere magic always requires the use of an actual magical resource (Tass) that is consumed. So it is a declining resource. Sorcerers may know Paths that actually do not work for them because they do not have any Tass available to make the magic work. Certain Paths still continue to work fine without the need for Tass because there is no Paradox issues with it. But if you want to use Hellfire, Flight, or some other power that would make people go &quot;that's magic!&quot; if they saw it, then that Sorcerer better have a source of something that provides Tass for them. The benefit of being a vampire who knows Thaumaturgy is that vitae is Tass and a vampire always has it, so it avoids that problem of a declining resource.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 12-19-2022, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T19:42:15-08:00","id":1499110,"title":"","content":"Numina is knowledge and or belief and you don't lose that during an embrace. And because of their studies in the occult, if their hedge-magic was similar to a vampire-thaumaturgy path, they can learn it as if they were Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T23:27:19-08:00","id":1499127,"title":"","content":"I tend to say you get in a clan discipline merit relavent to your paths. The only exceptions is purely altruistic powers which you just loose.<br /> <br /> As a side with mages I tend to suggest a trauma based derrangment on top of that. The fall is from a far greater height than the sleepers afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-08-2022, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T00:09:04-08:00","id":1499128,"title":"","content":"It's also worth considering letting sorcerers or mages that were members of certain factions start on a Path instead of Humanity. Plenty of them have philosophies far more in-line with the Paths than normal Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T06:53:51-08:00","id":1499141,"title":"","content":"This is a question that is actually answered in the original <i>Sorcerer</i> supplement from 1997 (p.54-56).<br /> <br /> If a Sorcerer becomes a Mage or Vampire, they can use their dots in Paths and Rituals to either buy Spheres or Blood Magic Paths on a 1-to-1 ratio. Or else cash them in for Freebie Points. The book even includes a chart showing what Sorcerer Paths could turn into. (It also suggests Arcanoi for Wraiths, in a narrative sense, but is very clear that all dots or XP are lost upon death, requiring a start from square one).<br /> <br /> This transition is not instantaneous. Rather requiring a period of adjustment, as the former Sorcerer comes to terms with their new state of being and adapts their old methods to the new supernatural framework that governs them. The book gives the timeframe as &quot;six months or more&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also a list of suggestions for how the more specialist splats might or might not adapt Sorcery. But it needs to be taken with a grain of salt, as it includes characters of <i>World of Darkness: [Ethnic Slur]</i> among the choices. I'm honestly surprised White Wolf still hadn't disowned that book by the time they were developing <i>Sorcerer</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T10:40:22-08:00","id":1499150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499069#post1499069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As an aside, in my own chronicles I rule that Sorcery Paths whose effects would be something that would invalidated by Paradox if it was Sphere magic always requires the use of an actual magical resource (Tass) that is consumed. So it is a declining resource. Sorcerers may know Paths that actually do not work for them because they do not have any Tass available to make the magic work.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting change in the basic / normal rules. Are there any other noteworthy differences, challanges, benefits, or advantages for Sorcerors in your chronicles?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499128#post1499128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plenty of them have philosophies far more in-line with the Paths than normal Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> This concept / idea certainly has merit, but I think that in regard to this it is important to note the fact that many Roads (be it Road of Kings or the Road of Sin) and Paths (be it the Path of Caine or the Path of Lilith) are constructed and practiced with a specific focus, distinct atmosphere, unique / characteristic attitude and particular intensity that might make them in many ways exclusive to the Kindred.<br /> <br /> As for other supernatural persons, perhaps Revenants - be it Obertus Revenants or Grimaldi Revenants - and also of course Ghouls should be though about first in regard to this.<br /> <br /> Other than Vampires, Ghouls, and Revenants, it might be extremely difficult for Sorcerors or Mages (including of course: Technocrats, Penny Dreadful's Gothic Romanticism Craft, or Mages from various other Crafts) to assure, claim, and develop various intelectual gains and situational benefits from following / being on a Road or a Path of Enlightenment. Or from directly and honestly supporting a Kindred on a Road or a Path in regard the methods, concepts, feelings, emotions, and ideas of a particular Road or a Path of Enlightenment. Even starting to follow - or reseraching - a particular Philosophy or Morality might be difficult, costly, or troublesome for a Mage or a Sorceror. Perhaps such decisinos and events can happen otherwise / differently if a Vampire or a Ghoul is asked for reliable, planned out, and honest advice, help, and support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-08-2022, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T18:27:11-08:00","id":1499182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499150#post1499150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting change in the basic / normal rules. Are there any other noteworthy differences, challanges, benefits, or advantages for Sorcerors in your chronicles?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only used Sorcerers as NPCs. They can make great antagonists, mentors, allies, contacts, rivals, etc. The players have always had standard PCs for whatever game. While I keep Mage metaphysics, I personally prefer to use Sorcerers as NPCs as they better fit what I need those NPCs to do. The changes I made was just to preserve the general idea in early WoD that &quot;magic was dying&quot;, keep the Sorcerer rules intact, but not allow them to be better in way than Mages by avoiding Paradox. If they could do that with static magic, I wanted it to cost them and not always work. So limiting the Paths that always work to things that could be ignored or discounted by Sleepers was good. I still wanted the option to use the more blatant magical Paths, but keep it consistent with what I thought better fit the setting, so making them dependent on some form of Tass to create these effects seemed obvious to me. <br /> <br /> It also provides a source of conflict if needed. If vampire vitae allows vampires to use Thaumaturgy, then it can also be used by Sorcerers as Tass to do the same for example. It isn't the only source of Tass out there, but some Sorcerers might want to exploit one or more vampires to gain access to that. Likewise, being able to harvest a tooth or fang from a Garou, or steal a real Fetter from a Wraith can provide real benefits to a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> I also think it flavors the game a lot to show certain Sorcerers dependent on &quot;components&quot;. Someone who knows Shapechanging can be dependent on only one form by that old wolfskin magically prepared centuries again and require him to create a salve using wolfsbane, henbane, etc. Steal grave soil if you actually want to be able to cross over into the Shadowlands or force a ghost to actually become visible in the Skinlands, and so on. Know when harvesting certain plants in the right conditions and times actually produce usable Tass rather than just having normal plants. I try to depict magic more like how the Call of Cthulhu encourages you to depict spells rather than D&amp;D style, &quot;I cast it and the effect happens&quot;. It does require more work as an ST, but this is an aspect of the game that I really like and have access to a lot of great books like the old Time-Life series The Enchanted World.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I don't think many players would like it if they wanted to play Sorcerers as PCs because it's a handicap and players tend to not like that. It's more important for them to get stuff done and accomplish things in game, rather than concentrating on creating neat flavor text. I certainly would not allow a Sorcerer PC alongside a standard vampire coterie or werewolf pack of PCs. But if I ever ran a mortals only game, I think it could work, and would be a good way to balance out a Sorcerer PC versus those PCs who might only have a single Numina or just be your standard detective, antiquarian, etc. with no powers at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T09:44:18-08:00","id":1499289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499182#post1499182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also provides a source of conflict if needed. If vampire vitae allows vampires to use Thaumaturgy, then it can also be used by Sorcerers as Tass to do the same for example. It isn't the only source of Tass out there, but some Sorcerers might want to exploit one or more vampires to gain access to that. Likewise, being able to harvest a tooth or fang from a Garou, or steal a real Fetter from a Wraith can provide real benefits to a Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be useful and nice if there would more descriptions and outlines in regard to how Vampires (and also Ghouls, or persons such as Obertus Revenants, Bratovitch Revenants, or Rafastio Revenants) can aid and also help Sorcerors and Mages in regard to research and spellcasting. Surely there are some particular ways of advising and supporting spellcasters that would be specific to Deathless / Vitae-based / Vampiric supernatural persons. Certainly meetings between persons belonging to different supernatural kinds / species / types can be entertaining, interesting, and also valueable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T10:39:18-08:00","id":1499291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499289#post1499289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be useful and nice if there would more descriptions and outlines in regard to how Vampires (and also Ghouls, or persons such as Obertus Revenants, Bratovitch Revenants, or Rafastio Revenants) can aid and also help Sorcerors and Mages in regard to research and spellcasting. Surely there are some particular ways of advising and supporting spellcasters that would be specific to Deathless / Vitae-based / Vampiric supernatural persons. Certainly meetings between persons belonging to different supernatural kinds / species / types can be entertaining, interesting, and also valueable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer Revised had the Blood Magic flaw (erroneously labeled a Merit). Where the character needed to use their blood (in the form of unsoakable Bashing damage) in order to cast spells.<br /> <br /> One of the potential explanations for the flaw was having learned magic from a vampire, or having plundered their books. Meaning, at least in regards to linear practitioners, if you were taught sorcery from a vampire, physical and/or metaphysical requirements peculiar to the vampiric condition color the Sorcerer's arts. A Mage could have the flexibility to invent a Rote that circumvents the more grisly or bloody aspects of vampiric magic, but a Sorcerer may not have that option. At least, not without buying off the flaw later.<br /> <br /> The flaw also states that, owing to the sanguine nature of the character's magic, their spells have a dark or &quot;martyred&quot; nature. This, more than anything, would probably carry over even into a Mage's castings, depending on how closely they're replicating the vampire's methods and/or the nature of the desired Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T05:54:14-08:00","id":1499642,"title":"","content":"Like Bluecho says, Numina will either convert to Thaumaturgy. Merits, or XP (preferably in that order) with perhaps a recovery time frame where the body needs to adjust to it's new state (I would posit that six months is too long, and something more incremental would be desirable.) <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I don't run Sorcery and Thaumaturgy as different things. Thaumaturgy can't be used when in frenzy because it's not a vampire power, it's entirely a matter of human knowledge and willpower. It's diametrically opposite Protean, which is the Beast manifest (making Settites super interesting, because they're heavily into both) <br /> Vitae is just a really convenient fuel for such powers, but it's entirely possible for Vampires to use substitutes. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll reverse the order of wards for humans ( Demons/Ghosts should be the easiest things for people to protect from since they're the most dependent on magic for their existence, ghouls should be really difficult because they're almost humans)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T12:05:45-08:00","id":1499671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499642#post1499642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I don't run Sorcery and Thaumaturgy as different things. Thaumaturgy can't be used when in frenzy because it's not a vampire power, it's entirely a matter of human knowledge and willpower. It's diametrically opposite Protean, which is the Beast manifest (making Settites super interesting, because they're heavily into both)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Followers of Set / Ministers / Setites are very interesting and nicely detailed and described, both as a Clan, and as various major and minor groups and organizations. And also of course as individual Vampiresses and Vampires described in particular World of Darkness / Vampire: the Masquerade guides / books.<br /> <br /> If it would be considered that the Protean Discipline is close to / related to the Beast (And maybe also overall to the more primal / wild aspects and qualities of Vampires), then what other Disciplines would you consider to also be part of this class \\ category? I clearly think that Potence, Celerity, Animalism, and also as well Fortitude would definitely belong to this category. But what about Obfuscate, Obtenebration, or Chimerstry? It does definitely seem that some analysis and interpretation are appropriate and possible in regard to this. <br /> <br /> Are there any additional or alternate terms / names / words for Kindred abilities and powers other than Discipline? Would any of these be good enough? Enchantment, Manifestation, Incantation?<br /> <br /> Also - do any of particular Disciplines have different / alternate terms or words which are clearly outlined as being in use by the Kindred when necessary or appropriate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T13:10:29-08:00","id":1499674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499642#post1499642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't run Sorcery and Thaumaturgy as different things. Thaumaturgy can't be used when in frenzy because it's not a vampire power, it's entirely a matter of human knowledge and willpower. It's diametrically opposite Protean, which is the Beast manifest (making Settites super interesting, because they're heavily into both)<br /> Vitae is just a really convenient fuel for such powers, but it's entirely possible for Vampires to use substitutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't personally agree with treating Thaumaturgy and Sorcery as completely interchangeable. I think magic has a connection to the soul, and there are significant differences between the souls of humans and Kindred that would warrant some shifts in the function and practice of magic as used by a human versus a vampire. That's precisely why a vampire loses their ability to use mortal Sorcery after the Embrace and has to re-develop their skills in the form of Thaumaturgy (generally; not really a fan of that one Merit from DAV). But that's not the old knowledge becoming useless but rather that it has to be adapted in certain respects while mostly remaining applicable.<br /> <br /> I do see the two as closely related, enough that a practitioner of one would probably be able to act as a half-decent mentor for the other, though there would be some subtle differences that the apprentice would need to figure out for themselves because the mentor just wouldn't be able to explain it (unless maybe the mentor is a vampire who replaced their mortal Sorcery with Thaumaturgy; then they would have experience with both and would understand the differences properly).<br /> <br /> A related topic: I can't recall for certain whether RAW supports a Ghoul being able to learn Thaumaturgy in theory, even if most sane vampires would never entrust that much power to one (I feel like some sources definitely support it, but they may have been retconned). It'd be grossly inefficient from a XP standpoint, but it seems like a Ghoul could learn both Sorcery and Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of a thaumaturge being able to learn how to use alternative sources of Mana/Quintessence instead of their own Vitae is a really neat idea, one I would probably be willing to explore in my own games. I'd imagine that other kinds of magical blood would probably be a good place to start, and then work your way out from there to other sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T23:06:22-08:00","id":1499722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499671#post1499671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If it would be considered that the Protean Discipline is close to / related to the Beast (And maybe also overall to the more primal / wild aspects and qualities of Vampires), then what other Disciplines would you consider to also be part of this class \\ category? I clearly think that Potence, Celerity, Animalism, and also as well Fortitude would definitely belong to this category. But what about Obfuscate, Obtenebration, or Chimerstry? It does definitely seem that some analysis and interpretation are appropriate and possible in regard to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the common disciplines (Animalism,Auspex,Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, Potence,Presence, Obfuscate) are extensions of human power: Humans can be strong, persuasive, perceptive and so on. On the otherhand, Things like Dominate or Obfuscate play on humanity's obedience and willfull ignorance, and you can argue it's the beast taking advantage of human nature. So for the core powers, I'd say they're probably 50/50. <br /> <br /> Chimistry, Obtenebration, Diamonion? Neither man nor beast; These are stolen powers. Chimistry belongs to Fae, Diamonion from demons, Obtenebration from the Abyss. Man willing to adapt anything to his advantage and the Beast is all too happy to facilitate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there any additional or alternate terms / names / words for Kindred abilities and powers other than Discipline? Would any of these be good enough? Enchantment, Manifestation, Incantation?<br /> <br /> Also - do any of particular Disciplines have different / alternate terms or words which are clearly outlined as being in use by the Kindred when necessary or appropriate? </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. The current discipline names are mostly just obscure/archaic English words. It stands to reason that non-english speaking countries at the least would use different words. Not to mention vampires don't exactly share information easily and need to keep the masquerade and so some local peculiarities/euphemisms are going to be a common feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T09:50:36-08:00","id":1499952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499047-embracing-a-sorcerer?p=1499722#post1499722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the common disciplines (Animalism,Auspex,Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, Potence,Presence, Obfuscate) are extensions of human power: Humans can be strong, persuasive, perceptive and so on. On the otherhand, Things like Dominate or Obfuscate play on humanity's obedience and willfull ignorance, and you can argue it's the beast taking advantage of human nature. So for the core powers, I'd say they're probably 50/50.<br /> <br /> Chimistry, Obtenebration, Diamonion? Neither man nor beast; These are stolen powers. Chimistry belongs to Fae, Diamonion from demons, Obtenebration from the Abyss. Man willing to adapt anything to his advantage and the Beast is all too happy to facilitate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Absolutely. The current discipline names are mostly just obscure/archaic English words. It stands to reason that non-english speaking countries at the least would use different words. Not to mention vampires don't exactly share information easily and need to keep the masquerade and so some local peculiarities/euphemisms are going to be a common feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just wandering - do any Camarilla Kindred or Anarch Vampires speak (and also ruminate, dream, think, and consider) - to at least some extent - in a language or using words and phrases that are purely and solely used by Vampires (and maybe by Ghouls, Revenants, and very rarely by other supernatural persons) and derived directly from Vampires' culture, outlooks, rules, laws, concepts, and philosophies? Or is it just the supernatural persons in the Tal'Mahe'Ra Sect, and maybe some of the Cainites from the Sabbat, who have specific language(s) and dialects created and used by Deathless / Vampiric supernatural persons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:30:14-08:00","id":1499978,"title":"","content":"There are probably vampires who have built a Conlang or code to communicate in secret. But I highly doubt it's a widespread practice. You would need to assume every vampire spreads knowledge of it to other vampires, or that loads of vampires would bother learning it. Plenty would see the utility, but not so much actually do it. At the very least, you wouldn't have anything resembling a unified Vampire Conlang, as Cainites throughout history were separated by thousands of miles and thousands of years.<br /> <br /> All this setting aside that the wider a secret language spreads, the more likely it is to filter into mortal parlance. Among secretive sects like the Tal'Mahe'Ra or Inconnu, you might see Conlangs used. But outside that, we're looking at very localized secret languages used by specific circles or communities of vampires and their trusted servants.<br /> <br /> Making a language whole cloth is a lot of work. Whereas we're more likely to see vampires just use <i>dead</i> languages. Tongues so archaic they escape mortal use, or are so rare as to be functionally dead for the purposes of guarding their secrets. This is more likely because, unlike a wholly constructed language, vampires can simply continue to use languages they're already accustomed to speaking from their mortal lives. Sires teach their Childer to speak these old tongues because it makes them more comfortable (even as the Sires seek instruction in modern lingo from their Childer, the better to fit in).<br /> <br /> Although, again, we'd see many different dead tongues proliferate, rather than any single one. Certain tongues may predominate, like Roman Latin, simply due to how widespread they are. But, especially with Latin, a language that spread too far becomes less useful as a cipher. There ARE people who read and speak Latin, even today. Really, while a common Lingua Franca is useful for mortals as a means of facilitating communication, an <i>uncommon</i> tongue is useful for stymieing understanding among those outside the know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}